      "id": 15,
      "options": {
        "content": "Use `trace_id` from a Policy Search completion log to open the matching Tempo trace. Compare request latency with Elasticsearch duration, then inspect the fixed `registered` and `terminated` worker signals. Legitimate idle time has zero request/event rates, present Go runtime samples, enabled state matching configuration, and zero in-flight age. An available deployment without a runtime sample is missing telemetry; rising shared drop, failure, lag, or queue signals indicate collection failure. Worker state is bounded to event type and never exposes queries, policy/customer data, topics, groups, credentials, arbitrary errors, or trace IDs as labels.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "Investigation workflow",
      "type": "text"
    }
